'''''Rhoicissus''''' is an [[Afrotropical realm|Afrotropical]] plant genus in the grape family [[Vitaceae]] and subfamily [[Vitoideae]]. There are between nine and twenty-two accepted species.<ref>{{cite web|title=Rhoicissus|url=http://www.theplantlist.org/tpl/search?q=Rhoicissus |work=The Plant List |date=2010 |accessdate=27 August 2013}}</ref><ref name=grin1/><ref name=grin2>{{ cite web |url=http://www.ars-grin.gov/cgi-bin/npgs/html/splist.pl?10419 |title=Species in GRIN for genus ''Rhoicissus'' |author=GRIN |work=Taxonomy for Plants |publisher=USDA, ARS, National Genetic Resources Program |location=National Germplasm Resources Laboratory, Beltsville, Maryland |accessdate=December 13, 2009}}</ref>

The leaves of species ''[[Rhoicissus tomentosa|R. tomentosa]]'' and ''R. tridentata'' are eaten by [[caterpillar]]s of the [[Hippotion celerio|silver striped hawkmoth]] (''Hippotion celerio'').<ref name=bde>{{ cite web |url=http://www.biodiversityexplorer.org/plants/vitaceae/rhoicissus.htm |title=''Rhoicissus'' |work=Biodiversity Explorer |publisher=[[Iziko Museum]]s of [[Cape Town]]|accessdate=December 13, 2009}}</ref>

